{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hi, mister. Washington, come on back. Before we get going, can you confirm your full name and date of birth for me?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 6.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Darnell Washington, February 9, 1968.",
   "start": 7.04,
   "end": 10.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Perfect thank you. How was the drive -in? I heard the parking garage was full again this morning.",
   "start": 11.8,
   "end": 17.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Oh, it was. I circled three times and ended up on the street two blocks down.",
   "start": 17.87,
   "end": 23.21
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Sorry about that, so this is your blood pressure follow -up. How have things been since we saw you in July?",
   "start": 23.77,
   "end": 28.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "pretty good mostly I've been checking it at home like you said and it's still kind of high usually like 145 150 on the top number",
   "start": 28.99,
   "end": 39.93
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "okay that's helpful and what are you taking for it right now",
   "start": 39.93,
   "end": 43.63
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "the listen April 10 milligrams in the morning wait no it's 20 you bumped it up last time remember I've got the new bottle in the car.",
   "start": 43.63,
   "end": 53.07
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Right twenty milligrams once a day. Are you taking it every day?",
   "start": 53.77,
   "end": 57.37
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Every day. I keep it next to the coffee maker so I don't forget.",
   "start": 58.06,
   "end": 62.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good trick and you're still on the atorvastatin for your cholesterol.",
   "start": 62.72,
   "end": 65.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, forty milligrams at night. That one I never miss.",
   "start": 66.76,
   "end": 70.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great, any headaches, chest pain or trouble catching your breath?",
   "start": 70.84,
   "end": 74.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, none of that.",
   "start": 74.96,
   "end": 76.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any dizziness when you stand up or swelling in your ankles.",
   "start": 76.76,
   "end": 79.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, but?",
   "start": 80.2,
   "end": 80.86
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any cough since you've been on the listen, April. Some people get a dry, tickly cough with it.",
   "start": 81.38,
   "end": 86.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Nah, no cough.",
   "start": 86.9,
   "end": 87.8
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How about salt? Last time you said you eat out a lot for lunch.",
   "start": 88.42,
   "end": 91.8
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Um, yeah, still work lunches. Lots of deli sandwiches and chips. I know, I know.",
   "start": 92.54,
   "end": 97.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And alcohols.",
   "start": 98.74,
   "end": 99.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A couple beers on the weekend, that's about it.",
   "start": 100.08,
   "end": 103.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, and you mentioned your dad before, right?",
   "start": 103.92,
   "end": 106.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, my father had a stroke at 62. That's kind of why my wife Lorraine stays on me about all this.",
   "start": 106.8,
   "end": 113.5
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That makes sense. She's looking out for you. All right, your blood pressure today is 152 over 94. And when I rechecked it after you sat quietly for five minutes, it was 148 over 92. Pulse is 72. Weight is 214 pounds. That's up three pounds from July.",
   "start": 114.0,
   "end": 130.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's the Halloween candy starting early, I guess.",
   "start": 131.4,
   "end": 134.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Let me take a listen, heart sounds regular no murmurs, lungs are clear and no swelling in your legs. I also have your labs from last week. Your potassium was 4 .4 and your kidney function was normal, create a 9 .0 .9. And your LDL cholesterol was 88.",
   "start": 134.94,
   "end": 151.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Is that good?",
   "start": 152.84,
   "end": 153.62
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "The cholesterol is right where we want it. And the kidneys and potassium look fine, which means we have room to go up on the listen -april. Okay. So here's what I'm thinking. Your blood pressure is still above our goal of under 130 over 80, even on the 20 milligrams. I'd like to increase the listen -up to 40 milligrams once a day. Until you run out, you can take two of your 20s together in the morning.",
   "start": 154.32,
   "end": 179.31
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Two of the 20s, got it.",
   "start": 179.75,
   "end": 181.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Keep the adorv acid in the same 40 milligrams at night. I'd also like you to cut back on salt, aim for less than 2 ,000 milligrams a day. The deli meat and chips are big ones.",
   "start": 182.29,
   "end": 192.81
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I can try packing lunch, Lorraine will be thrilled.",
   "start": 193.43,
   "end": 196.41
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That would help a lot. Since we're raising the dose, I want to repeat potassium and kidney check in about two weeks. You can go to our lab on Brookfield Avenue, no appointment needed.",
   "start": 197.3,
   "end": 206.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I'm off on the 19th, does that work?",
   "start": 207.72,
   "end": 210.14
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "The 19th is perfect. Keep checking at home and bring your log next time. If you get readings over 180 on the top, or a severe headache, chest pain or weakness on one side, call us or go to the emergency room.",
   "start": 210.82,
   "end": 223.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "We'll do.",
   "start": 223.96,
   "end": 224.5
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And I'll see you back in six weeks. Is your cell still 555 -0163?",
   "start": 225.18,
   "end": 230.06
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yep, same number.",
   "start": 231.16,
   "end": 232.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 38,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great any other questions for me?",
   "start": 232.96,
   "end": 234.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 39,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, I think that's it. Thanks, Dark.",
   "start": 235.26,
   "end": 237.5
  },
  {
   "idx": 40,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Take care, Darnell. Good luck with the parking on the way out. out.",
   "start": 238.26,
   "end": 241.6
  }
 ],
